A hand-filed item in a vault without an open-items directory becomes `OI-0001`: the directory
is created, the file carries the flags, `status: open`, null plan and closure keys and the
stubbed date, and stdout is its vault-relative path alone.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  core.macros.date: "2026-10-15"
-- cmd --
booping items add --title "Spec the tracker" --direction code-to-spec --text "Two lines of prose."
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
open-items/OI-0001.md
-- stderr --
-- expected/cwd/vault/open-items/OI-0001.md --
---
id: OI-0001
title: "Spec the tracker"
status: open
direction: code-to-spec
record: null
source: manual
plan: null
created_at: 2026-10-15
closed_at: null
reason: null
---

# Spec the tracker

Two lines of prose.
